@HELP: Commands -- / and TSO                    !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
@  /}command     }gives an MVS or JES2 command as from the master console.
}
}  Examples: /D A,L or /$DI. The answer goes to the system log: give the
}  command on the LOG panel to see it there. The panel says COMMAND
}  ISSUED. / alone: NO COMMAND PROVIDED.
}
}  Operator commands need UPDATE access to SDSF.OPER (topic 13 of the
}  contents); without it: NOT AUTHORIZED FOR CMD.
}
@  TSO}command   }runs a TSO command, CLIST or program.
}
}  Example: TSO LISTCAT. The screen shows what the command writes; after
}  Enter the SDSF panel comes back. TSO alone: COMMAND PARM IS MISSING.
}
}  The command line is as long as the screen leaves room for: 42
}  characters on a screen 80 columns wide.
}
}
}
}
